---
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Cody Duke cover letter for Product Designer at Tiny Health."
    />
    <title>Cody Duke, Product Designer Cover Letter</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={withBase('/favicon.svg')} />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://api.fontshare.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://api.fontshare.com/v2/css?f[]=clash-grotesk@500,600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Figtree:wght@500;600;700&family=Source+Serif+4:opsz,wght@8..60,400;8..60,500;8..60,600&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <p class="letter-chrome">
      <a href={withBase('/')}>← Portfolio</a>
      <button type="button" onclick="window.print()">Print / Save PDF</button>
    </p>

    <article class="letter">
      <header class="letter__header">
        <div>
          <h1>Cody Duke</h1>
          <p class="letter__role">Product Designer</p>
          <p class="letter__location">Orem, Utah, open to remote</p>
        </div>
        <address>
          <a href="tel:+15013395093">(501) 339-5093</a>
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
          <a href={withBase('/')}>Portfolio</a>
          <a href={site.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
        </address>
      </header>

      <p class="letter__meta">August 18, 2026</p>
      <p class="letter__meta">Tiny Health hiring team</p>
      <p class="letter__meta">Product Designer</p>

      <div class="letter__body">
        <p>
          I am applying for the Product Designer role at Tiny Health. Your product has to make
          complex science feel trustworthy enough that a family will act on it. That is the design
          work I want to do, and the work I have been doing.
        </p>
        <p>
          At FamilySearch, beginners arrived hoping to feel a connection to their family and met a
          toolbox built for hobbyists. I led product design for 26 personalized discovery
          experiences. Each one started from a person already in the tree (a name, a birthday, or a
          record) and offered one next action instead of a search lesson. Retention rose 95% for
          members and 107% for other users versus the prior year. A Tiny Health report has the same
          job. The value is not 120,000 microbes on a page. It is an expert highlight and an action
          plan a parent can actually follow.
        </p>
        <p>
          At Entrata I spent seven years on that same problem with production data, field research,
          and engineering partners. That included Homebody, a resident-facing mobile app that
          reached 4.4 out of 5 on iOS from more than 600 reviews in its first six months; setup
          systems that had to stay accurate without getting harder to use; and AI flows that turned
          long paperwork into an upload. For about a year I was Product Lead with an owned
          engineering team, taking work from research through ship. I care more about whether people
          come back and act than whether the interface looks finished.
        </p>
        <p>
          I live in Orem, Utah, so the 9am to 6pm CST overlap window fits my day. I have not
          designed in DTC health. I have designed for families at scale, shipped consumer mobile,
          and sat with experts until the science, or the system, could be said in a sentence a real
          person would use.
        </p>
        <p>I would welcome the chance to walk you through the work.</p>
        <p class="letter__signoff">
          Sincerely,<br />
          Cody Duke
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    --resume-ink: #1c1c1a;
    --resume-muted: #5c5c56;
    --resume-line: rgba(28, 28, 26, 0.18);
    --resume-paper: #ffffff;
    --resume-field: #fbfbf1;
    --font-display: 'Clash Grotesk', 'Figtree', 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif;
    --font-ui: 'Figtree', 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif;
    --font-body: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
  }

  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  html,
  body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  body {
    background: var(--resume-field);
    color: var(--resume-ink);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
  }

  a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.14em;
  }

  .letter-chrome {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    max-width: 8.5in;
    margin: 1.25rem auto 0.75rem;
    padding: 0 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .letter-chrome button {
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--resume-ink);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--resume-line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.85rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .letter {
    width: 8.5in;
    min-height: 11in;
    margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
    padding: 0.48in 0.58in 0.42in;
    background: var(--resume-paper);
    color: var(--resume-ink);
    box-shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(28, 28, 26, 0.08);
  }

  .letter__header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.24in;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--resume-line);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 2.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    line-height: 0.95;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .letter__role {
    margin: 0.28rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--resume-muted);
  }

  .letter__location {
    margin: 0.22rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--resume-muted);
  }

  address {
    margin: 0;
    font-style: normal;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    text-align: right;
    color: var(--resume-muted);
  }

  address a {
    display: block;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.16em;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(28, 28, 26, 0.35);
  }

  .letter__meta {
    margin: 0.18in 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--resume-muted);
  }

  .letter__meta + .letter__meta {
    margin-top: 0.08rem;
  }

  .letter__body {
    margin-top: 0.28in;
  }

  .letter__body p {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.48;
  }

  .letter__signoff {
    margin-top: 1.15rem !important;
  }

  @media print {
    @page {
      size: letter;
      margin: 0;
    }

    html,
    body {
      background: white;
    }

    .letter-chrome {
      display: none;
    }

    .letter {
      margin: 0;
      box-shadow: none;
      min-height: 11in;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 900px) {
    body {
      background: var(--resume-paper);
    }

    .letter {
      width: auto;
      min-height: 0;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 2.5rem;
      box-shadow: none;
    }

    .letter__header {
      display: block;
    }

    .letter__header address {
      text-align: left;
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
